<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<map xmlns="http://openorienteering.org/apps/mapper/xml/v2" version="9">
    <notes>INFO (course setter to include on map)
Title:
	Northern part: Spencerville
	Western part: Bottle Lake
	South-Eastern part: Pegasus
Scale: 1:15,000
Contour interval: 2.5m
North lines: 300m apart


CREDITS (course setter to include on map - 6pt Arial)
Cartography: M. Wood 2007
Remapped by B. Teahan 2019
Combined by R. Moore 2022`
Updates: G. Smith 2011, M. Smithson T. Wright 2012, S. Smith P. Cleary T. Cambridge L. Earnshaw 2014, C. Jørgensen M. Smithson 2016
Copyright © Peninsula and Plains Orienteers
Possession of this map does not imply right of access
Non-commercial use only unless otherwise granted
Map version: dc64bb7


COORDINATORS' NOTES (map coordinator to update + commit on map being sent)
Last sent to: Angus Laird &lt;angus.laird@icloud.com&gt;


CONTROLLERS' NOTES (controller to read upon map being sent)
All courses need to be approved 2-3 weeks before event with CCC (see permissions).
Hazards include traffic, mountain bikers, pedestrians, lake, river, prickly bushes, cliffs, horses.
The park rangers at the spencerville end of the park are extremely helpful and responsive. Best to make initial contact either via phone or in person. They like to know who they are dealing with.

Access:
They seem quite relaxed about access into the park for both people and vehicels. This is subject to fire danger.
Golf road of Hyders road provides a nice entry point. It would pay to check the raod you intend to drive donw some are quite over grown. If you aare unlonking a gate to let competitors in then count in having some one stationed at the gate while it is unlocked.

Spencer Park Ranger:
Steve Leiataua - &lt;Steve.Leiataua@ccc.govt.nz&gt;
Work - 03 941 7560
Mobile - 0272267450
Deals specifficaly with spencer park

Bottle Lake Forest Manager:
Warren Hunt &lt;Warren.Hunt@ccc.govt.nz&gt;
Mobile - 027 475 9708
Deals with the commerical forest area outside of spencer park. Less communicative than Steve.

The area to the east between the bottom of spencer park and 13th marks as slow running is starting to open up. The broom has mostly died off and is easily crush at this point. it will quickly become runable and provides a lot of good navigations challenges.
The main forestry blocks can be quite variable with light blackberry cover poping you at random.


MAPPERS' NOTES
Landowner: Christchurch City Council
Forest manager: Raynoier / Matariki Forests

Nick Smith - 
A few more comments about Bottle Lake:

- I got round 95% of the map but there were a couple of corners of the map and tracks that I didn't get. It looked like a small amount of logging was ongoing in the middle of the map too around the dump area.

- I have marked the section at the Spencerville end that I think would be good to update further if there is a major event. Quite flat on the west side but with enough contours and vegetation to make it interesting. 

- I updated/moved more of the contours towards the north end in the open white blocks than I thought I would when I last emailed you. I mainly moved the existing contours but then reshaped the larger contour features.  

- The vegetation in this area I have done generally, if someone was remapping from scratch they can probably do some more detail. Overall I updated the north end enough to be usable even if a little rough around the edges. 

- Consistency issues with the green stripe. Sometimes the green stripe is for tree trimmings/fellings which you can get through at walking pace in a straight line, but some of the other bits denote bramble crap which you can get through but you might have to take a detour round patches of brambles. No good fix but just something to note.  

I wouldn't say updating the north end of the map is the highest priority, it can be used as is. However if you line a couple of decent events to use the map, eg. Canterbury Schools this year and then QBD next year maybe then I think it would be well worth doing. 
</notes>
